## What this predicate means

**A `demonstrated-by` B** — B demonstrates A (inverse of `demonstrates`).  The author-side advertisement: "this concept / pattern / contract has known illustrations at B."

Common shapes:
- A pattern demonstrated-by an example memorial
- A library demonstrated-by a code-walkthrough
- A protocol demonstrated-by a session-log of running it

